== Undergraduate Research and Work Experience

~~~
{}{img_left}{assets/Apple/logo2.png}{Apple Logo}{250}{250}{}
*Apple iOS Location and Motion SWE Intern* \n\n
Summer 2015 \n\n

I spent a summer working at Apple. It was my first experience working with deep learning models like CNNs. I was very fortunate to have [https://research.fb.com/people/gauci-jason/ Jason Gauci] as my mentor - I learned a great deal from him. I also had the opportunity to present my work to [https://www.apple.com/leadership/craig-federighi/ Craig Federighi], which was awesome. 
~~~

~~~
{}{img_left}{assets/CHIC/logo.png}{CHIC logo}{250}{250}{}
*Caltech High-Speed Integrated Circuits* \n\n
Summer 2014 \n\n

I spent a summer working in the [https://chic.caltech.edu/ Caltech High-Speed Integrated Circuits] lab under [https://chic.caltech.edu/hajimiri/ Professor Ali Hajimiri]. I implemented a feedback loop consisting of both hardware and software interfaces, allowing for a wireless power transfer prototype. You can find a video about some of the latest developments on the project below. 

\[[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d1_2CkUdnT4 video]] 
~~~

~~~
{}{img_left}{assets/SLAC/logo.png}{SLAC logo}{250}{250}{}
*SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory* \n\n
Summer 2013 \n\n

I spent a summer working at the [https://www6.slac.stanford.edu/ SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory] under [https://web.stanford.edu/dept/app-physics/cgi-bin/person/tor-o-raubenheimer/ Professor Tor O. Raubenheimer] and [https://profiles.stanford.edu/juhao-wu Dr. Juhao Wu]. I investigated whether harmonic lasing could be used to make the shift towards higher energy radiation. This was my first research experience - I was very fortunate to have [https://web.stanford.edu/dept/app-physics/cgi-bin/person/tor-o-raubenheimer/ Professor Tor O. Raubenheimer] and [https://profiles.stanford.edu/juhao-wu Dr. Juhao Wu] as mentors who took time to teach me how to approach difficult scientific problems. 

\[[assets/SLAC/Final_draft.pdf report]] \[[https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0168900216311901 publication]] 
~~~

== Undergraduate Projects

~~~
{}{img_left}{assets/EE52/fig.png}{MP3 Player Figure}{250}{250}{}
*Blackfin MP3 Player* \n\n
Winter and Spring 2014

I built an MP3 player over 2 quarters in sophomore year for our embedded systems project class. By far the most difficult thing I have ever had to do. It even almost worked. You can find an extensive report (aka the longest thing I've ever written) below. Thanks [https://directory.caltech.edu/personnel/gleng Glen]!

\[[assets/EE52/documentation.pdf report]]
~~~

~~~
{}{img_left}{assets/CS156b/fig.jpg}{Netflix Figure}{250}{250}{}
*Netflix Challenge* \n\n
Spring 2015 \n\n

A couple of my friends and I competed took a project class where we had to essentially participate in the Netflix Challenge. We leveraged a Netflix dataset of user-movie ratings to build a recommender system. This was a great experience in implementing models from papers and working with large datasets. We placed 3rd in our class. 

\[[assets/CS156b/presentation.pdf presentation]]
~~~

~~~
{}{img_left}{assets/EE91/fig.png}{Function Generator Figure}{250}{250}{}
*Analog Function Generator* \n\n
Winter 2016 \n\n

I built an analog function generator from scratch for a project in senior year! It can generate a square wave, a triangle wave, and a sine wave with different voltage amplitudes and frequencies.

\[[assets/EE91/report.pdf report]]
~~~

~~~
{}{img_left}{assets/EE90/fig.png}{Smart Dog Bowl Figure}{250}{250}{}
*Smart Dog Bowl* \n\n
Spring 2015 \n\n

I built a dog bowl that can open automatically when a special IR tag (worn by a dog) comes close enough.

\[[assets/EE90/report.pdf report]]
~~~

